# ROOT CAUSE of "Build sandboxing disabled due to nsjail error.": nsjail is present in the tree and
# works, but it opens every component of the source path with O_RDONLY|O_DIRECTORY while assembling the
# sandbox mount tree. On this host the tree lives under /serverhive5, which the provider owns with mode
# 0711 (traverse-only, root-owned) and we have no root to change, so that open fails with EACCES -
# reproduced directly: `nsjail -R / -R /serverhive5/chenpan -- /bin/true` fails in
# createDirRecursively() on 'serverhive5' with Permission denied, while the same command against /home
# succeeds. Soong then disables sandboxing and says so, on every build.
#
# This is a PRECONDITION TEST, not a suppression: the attempt is skipped only when the path is provably
# unreadable, and sandboxing resumes automatically once it is readable again (provider grants read on
# the storage root, or the tree moves). The REAL fix on this host is one command for the provider:
#     chmod 755 /serverhive5
# which is recorded in the ledger as a request.
